course: dictionary
lesson: 2930
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and drawing is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. «Her drawing of the old lighthouse was pinned on the wall.» Here a drawing is a picture made with a pencil, pen or crayon, mostly with lines.
explain: Drawing can also mean the art or activity of making pictures. «Drawing helps Mia to think clearly, so she draws every morning.» Here drawing names what Mia does, not a picture she has made. Ask yourself: is it a thing you can hold, or something you do?
explain: Drawing can also be the -ing form of the verb draw. «Drawing a straight line needs a ruler.» «The crowd was drawing near as the bus pulled in.» Drawing near means coming closer. Look at the word after drawing: if it names an action, like a line or the curtains, then draw is the verb.
fact: Drawing can be a noun (a picture) or the -ing form of the verb draw.
fact: «Her broken-spear drawing becomes the sign for la.» Here drawing is a picture.
fact: «Chalk drawings belong on your own driveway or a quiet path, never on the road where cars come.» Chalk drawings are pictures made with chalk.
fact: Drawing near means coming closer, and drawing the curtains means closing them.
fact: Scale drawings and labelled drawings are used in school art, maths and science.
exercise: «Her broken-spear drawing becomes the sign for la.» In this sentence, what is a drawing? | *A picture made with lines | Someone drawing the curtains | A game of chance | A long walk
exercise: «The crowd was drawing near as the bus pulled in.» What does drawing near mean? | Leaving quickly | *Coming closer | Sleeping soundly | Pulling a picture
exercise: «She was drawing the curtains when the sun set.» What is the word drawing doing here? | It is a kind of paint | It is a name for an art class | *It is the -ing form of draw, an action | It is a picture on the wall
test: In «Chalk drawings belong on your own driveway», what kind of word is drawings? | Verb, an action word | *Noun, pictures made with chalk | Adjective, a describing word | Adverb, a how word
test: Which of these means drawing as an art or activity? | Drawing a raffle ticket | *Making pictures, like learning to paint and draw | A drawing pinned on the wall | Scale drawings for maths
exam: In «The drawing of a frog hung on the wall», what kind of word is drawing? | Adverb, a how word | Adjective, a describing word | Verb, an action word | *Noun, a picture
